<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ioannis Metaxas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1871">1871</a>–<a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ioannis Metaxas was a Greek general and politician who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> as dictator from 4 August 1936 until his death, with the support of King George II. His regime suspended parliament, imposed censorship and promoted a nationalist Third Hellenic Civilisation. In October 1940 he rejected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>'s ultimatum, bringing Greece into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ioannis-metaxas.jpg" alt="Ioannis Metaxas" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Archaeological Society at Athens / εν Aθήναις Aρχαιολογική Eταιρεία, 1937 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ioannis_Metaxas_1937_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A republic of 1924 fell to a royalist coup in 1935, and <b>Ioannis Metaxas</b>'s 4th of August Regime of 1936 opened an authoritarian era that lasted, through occupation and the civil war that ended in 1949, until 1974.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hellenic-republic">Hellenic Republic · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>A plebiscite restored George II in 1935, but in 1936 he allowed <b>Ioannis Metaxas</b> to establish a dictatorship.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece">Kingdom of Greece · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
